WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.368
-My first guest
is one of my favorites.

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.602
She's an Oscar-nominated actress

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:06.305
who stars in the new movie
"Superintelligence,"

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:09.208
which will be available
on HBO Max tomorrow.

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:13.446
Here is Melissa McCarthy.
Ah! There -- Come on.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.181
I am so happy to see you.
-Hi.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.383
-Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:20.119
I appreciate it.
I just was talking

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.988
to your husband, Ben Falcone,

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.756
who's the director
of this movie.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:28.228
And we were -- he was actually
sitting where you're sitting.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.728
-I know.
We're in the --

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:34.400
It kind of looks like I should
be just constantly gyroscoping.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.769
-It is a beautiful scene,
like you're in a wave

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.272
or it's, like,
a Chris Nolan-y type of vibe.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.474
-Exactly.
Chris is here with me.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.075
Yeah,
I just keep him off-camera.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:44.310
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.444
-He's quarantining
with you guys?

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.814
That's so cool.
-Yeah, for sure.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:50.149
-But you guys
are in Australia right now.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:51.750
-We are.
-So, you are currently

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.987
a day ahead of me.
You're living in the future.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:57.023
-Yes, I'm in your future.
You're doing great.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.425
-How's my day
gonna go tonight?

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.392
Am I gonna get
a good night's sleep?

00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:01.961
-No, you won't sleep.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:06.599
But, boy, you'll wake up,
still feeling renewed and fresh.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.434
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.337
-You'll have one
huge white streak, though.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.673
I won't explain it.
-Okay, no problem.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.642
Well, I sleep
with a lightning rod,

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.778
so I was just kind of hoping
for something to happen.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.112
I'm like,
"What a bad investment."

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:22.247
Well, tonight's the night.

00:01:22.247 --> 00:01:25.418
Right now, you're in the middle
of filming a new series.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.220
That's why you're in Australia.
-Yes.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.056
-And you are working with
all my favorite peeps.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:33.559
Nicole Kidman, Bobby Cannavale,
Michael Shannon.

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:36.396
I would go anywhere with --
And you!

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.831
Anywhere you guys
are showing up, I would go.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.667
What is -- What are you
shooting, and how is it going?

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:44.036
-It is so crazy.
It's such a good group.

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:46.572
And, like, everyone's so weird.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.741
-Which is always, like,
my favorite when you find it.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.477
'Cause I've met Nicole,
but I've not worked with her.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.346
And there's something
so regal about her.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:56.449
You expect her to be like,
"Hello. I'm Nicole Kidman."

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.518
And then,
you really get to know her,

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.119
and you're like,
"She's weird!"

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.388
She's, like, a wonderful weirdo.
-Yeah, she's fun.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.957
-And Michael Shannon,
who just --

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:07.926
I just literal hunker down,
and sometimes they're like,

00:02:07.926 --> 00:02:09.896
"Melissa, it's your line."
I'm like, "Oh, I'm sorry."

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.331
I was just --
I was just watching Shannon,

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:15.034
'cause he's one of
the most fascinating people

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.102
I've ever met.
And funniest.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.470
-And funny --
Oh, I was just gonna say.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.704
You beat me to it.

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:20.607
He's one of the funniest people
I've ever met.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.476
We were doing some bit here,
joking around, we were saying,

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.245
it was, like,
"Hey, it's National Cape Day.

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:28.714
We're all gonna wear capes."
Just made it up.

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:31.016
And, dude, he came out
in a full-on cape.

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:32.886
He went and found one
in the wardrobe department.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.788
A full-on vampire-like
Dracula cape.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.157
And didn't say --
-That could also be

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:40.759
how he goes to Trader Joe's.

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:42.161
You just don't know
what's gonna happen.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.229
-Yeah, he showed up
one time wearing

00:02:44.229 --> 00:02:46.599
an "Alvin and the Chipmunks"
onesie on my show.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.467
It was like, "Okay."
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.237
-And no explanation.
He's just fun, that's all.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:55.141
Are you getting any of the
Australian accent at all?

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:58.077
-I've got -- I think
the closest I'm coming to is,

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.481
I really love their "no's,"
because it's "ner."

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.882
-Yeah, you're right.
It is "ner."

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.918
-"Ner!"
They end it with an "R,"

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:08.053
and it's the best thing.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:12.392
And sometimes I'll say things
to try to get people to say no.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.961
"Ner."
And they say, "No drama.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.929
No drama."
And the first time somebody

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:19.732
said it,
I was asking somebody something,

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.367
because there's no COVID here.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.203
So, everyone's still
super careful, but you're --

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:28.474
we can be out among people,
delightfully so.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:32.378
And I was asking for something,
and someone goes, "No drama."

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.447
And I was like, "Oh, no, no, no!
There is no drama.

00:03:35.447 --> 00:03:38.818
I was just curious."
-"I don't want to start drama."

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.954
-"Yeah, yeah, no drama."
-"No, we're not making drama."

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.589
-I kept thinking
they were thinking I was, like,

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:45.158
flying off the handle.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:48.728
And then I just realized,
it's just what they say.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:53.466
But I kept re-explaining.
-"Ner drama."

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:57.303
I want to talk to you about
the movie "Superintelligence."

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.038
What a great, funny premise.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:02.374
But I really like the idea
that you and your husband

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:06.512
had this great idea to go along
with the release of the movie.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:09.549 line:0%
It's called
20 Days of Kindness.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.785 line:0%
And can you explain that
to everyone watching?

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.554
-Yeah, it's --
You know, we made this --

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:19.258
We actually shot this movie
almost 2 1/2 years ago.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:20.693
-Wow.
-And it was kind of strange

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.561
that when
it's finally now coming out,

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.563
it seems almost more relevant.

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:27.366
It seems like we wrote it
three weeks ago.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:30.536
And there's such a --
I mean, it really is,

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.539
people are worth saving,
love wins.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.774
And just talking about
we all kind of --

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:38.110
Even if it's just on Zoom,
we were coming back together.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.113
And it just felt like...

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:43.816
What's going on in the world
and what this movie stands for,

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.952
we're like, we can't just --
we want people to see the movie,

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:49.922
'cause I do think
it's so happy and funny

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.957
that it's what people kind of
need right now.

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:55.227
It's --
It's really warm-hearted.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.629
And we're like,
"We should do something

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.564
'cause we're lucky enough
to be putting this out."

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:03.102
So, we picked 20 charities, and
we're giving each one $20,000.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.804
And we've had --

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.605
And Girls Who Code
was our first one,

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:08.408
and AT&amp;T came in the first day

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.376
and gave them
an additional $1 million.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.445
-Oh, my goodness.
-And I think just

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:15.414
constantly checking in with
how many people even

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:18.116
during these crazy times

00:05:18.116 --> 00:05:20.819
are still putting all this time
into helping people.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:23.822
It's so inspiring.
It's really something.

00:05:23.822 --> 00:05:26.325
Today's our day 16.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:28.528
-What charity
are you highlighting today?

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.463
-Habitat for Humanity.
-Oh.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:33.099
-Which is --
I mean, you just --

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.936
They're constantly, constantly
finding and helping people.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.503
So...
-Oh, they need help.

00:05:38.503 --> 00:05:40.573
We love them.
Oh, it's great.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.608
I want to talk more about
the movie when we come back.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:45.411
Can you stick around
for five more minutes?

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.513
-No.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.315
-I know --
I already have --

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.550
I can call Ben.
I can call your husband.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.419
Now we're like old buddies now.
I have his cellphone.

